sqlparse-begin-end-semicolon.prompt:
sqlparse.split() cuts a statement apart at the semicolons inside a BEGIN ... END body. For example, splitting this SQL:

WITH
FUNCTION meaning_of_life()
  RETURNS tinyint
  BEGIN
    DECLARE a tinyint DEFAULT CAST(6 as tinyint);
    DECLARE b tinyint DEFAULT CAST(7 as tinyint);
    RETURN a * b;
  END
SELECT meaning_of_life();

returns 4 pieces ('WITH ... DECLARE a tinyint DEFAULT CAST(6 as tinyint);', 'DECLARE b ...;', 'RETURN a * b;', 'END\nSELECT meaning_of_life();'), but it is one statement and split() should return it as a single item. Please fix this without changing any other behavior.

mistune-list-directive-markers.prompt:
With md = mistune.create_markdown(escape=False, plugins=[FencedDirective([Admonition()], markers=':')]) (from mistune.directives), a line with a single colon like ':{note}' is literal text at the top level (md(':{note}
lazy
') gives '<p>:{note}
lazy</p>'), but right after a '- ' bullet item it opens an admonition: md('- item
:{note}
lazy
') renders '<ul><li>item</li></ul>' followed by '<section class="admonition note">...<p>lazy</p></section>'. A fenced directive needs at least three markers, so expected is no admonition and ':{note}' kept as text. A real ':::{note}' fence after a list item should still end the list and render the admonition. Please fix this without changing any other behavior.
